now  mourning a life lost too soon and in a  terrible way the killing of a  four-year-old boy is taking center stage  tonight good evening and thanks for  joining us here at six i'm denise valdez  and i'm brian loftis the family of the  four-year-old boy telling eight news now  his name is mason dominguez police tell  us the boy's body was found in a freezer  yesterday inside a home near the  intersection of lamb boulevard and kerry  avenue  now this is the man accused of that  crime brandon tosland he was in court  earlier on today he is facing open  murder charges in this case the victim  is one of his girlfriend's children  and there's a lot more to get to here we  do have team coverage tonight with  details you will only see right here on  8 news now first we're going to send it  over to david charns he has the latest  on the investigation david  brian denise the house where detectives  say this four-year-old's body was found  is dark tonight there is a truck parked  out front  investigators tell me in that truck  they found sand and debris from this  home's backyard now more on that in a  moment  first here's what we know about the  investigation into this child's burden  found in a freezer in a trash bag that's  how investigators say they discovered  four-year-old mason dominguez's body  inside this northeast valley home  we obviously have a report from auburn  35 year old brandon tozlund accused of  killing the boy in concealing his body  for at least two months he looked down  as prosecutors read aloud the details of  his girlfriend's son's death the  four-year-old victim in this particular  case was found deceased court documents  say toslin told the boy's mother that he  had found mason unconscious in december  they say the boy's body had visible  injuries but it's too soon to say just  how he died they say toslin told his  girlfriend mason was sick and that she  wasn't allowed to see the child we do  know from our interviews that the  suspect  is alleged to have been physical with  the victim and had spanked him  excessively on more than one occasion on  tuesday mason's sister handed a note to  a teacher saying she and her mother were  being held against their will court  documents alleging toslin tied up  mason's mother even handcuffing her when  they drove in a car  that eventually led to the discovery  tuesday of mason's body in the garage we  observed a very large hole inside the  backyard that appears to be that someone  was digging a grave  that hole is at least eight feet deep  and my colleague joe moeller will have  more on that part of this investigation  in just a moment tozland is due in court  again on monday  in terms of how mason died that remains  a big question tonight and one  investigators don't have the answer to  they say that will take several days  live near  carrion lamb tonight i'm david charns  live local now  david thank you for that now let's get  right over to joel moller he does  continue our team coverage he has been  talking to the family of the victim and  joe what do you know tonight  brian and denise we're on the sidewalk  here on lamb on the other side of this  wall right here is that eight foot deep  hole and metro police are now  investigating as a possible grave we  have a look at it from a neighbor's home  from the second story of that home  meanwhile the family of the victim's  father are now reacting to what happened  it is a chilling sight from a neighbor's  second story window you can see this big  hole police say they are investigating  as a possible grave neighbors tell me it  appeared a month and a half ago  basically overnight as the investigation  continues into the death of mason  dominguez his father's side of the  family is left heartbroken he was the  one that was going to carry on my  brother's  last name mason's father elijah  dominguez passed away from pneumonia in  january of 2021. we spoke to elijah's  sister shirona ruiz villalobos as she  was traveling from california she  described her nephew mason he was just  so full of joy like he was just as soon  as he was born he was just like the  light of all of our life it's just super  unfortunate that  he's wrong a little over a month after  elijah died she says mason's mother  dacia maldonado moved in with tozland at  this home i reached out multiple times  via text to  dossier and email just concerning the  whereabouts of my niece and nephew she  says the family knew toaslan before  elijah passed away but never thought  this could happen  questions linger especially about the  possible grave ruiz villalobo says she  wants to know about what was happening  inside this home and why little mason  was missing for so long i don't think  she's innocent how do you not know where  your child  [Music]  is now back out here live she also tells  me they set up a gofundme to get mason  buried by his father we have a link to  that up on our website eightnewsnow.com  reporting live joe mulder live local now  and don't forget there is help for  anyone who might be experiencing  domestic abuse local non-profit safe  nest offers a 24-hour confidential  hotline that you can call you can text  the phone number is on your screen at  702-646-4981  by the way the organization also  provides shelter and counseling

